### Variables
@host = http://localhost:8080

### 1) Le service externe reçoit une requête -> lance le workflow (1 "jour" = 10 s)
POST {{host}}/mock-api/requests
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "idRequest": "REQ-1001",
  "traderFirstName": "Test",
  "traderLastName": "Trader",
  "traderEmail": "trader@exemple.com",
  "marketId": "MKT01",
  "marketName": "Marché test",
  "testMode": true,
  "testIntervalSeconds": 10
}

### 2) Etat du workflow (tâches actives, variables)
GET {{host}}/api/requests/REQ-1001

### 3) Emails simulés
GET {{host}}/api/requests/REQ-1001/emails

### 4) "Assign to me" par alice
POST {{host}}/api/requests/REQ-1001/team/claim
Content-Type: application/json

{ "userId": "alice" }

### 5) Un autre opérateur essaie de prendre la même demande -> 409 attendu
POST {{host}}/api/requests/REQ-1001/team/claim
Content-Type: application/json

{ "userId": "bob" }

### 6) Submit SANS cocher la confirmation -> retour à la même tâche (nouvelle tâche non assignée)
POST {{host}}/api/requests/REQ-1001/team/submit
Content-Type: application/json

{ "userId": "alice", "confirmOnBehalf": false }

### 7) Re-claim puis Submit AVEC confirmation -> statut WAITING_TRADER + email trader
POST {{host}}/api/requests/REQ-1001/team/claim
Content-Type: application/json

{ "userId": "alice" }

###
POST {{host}}/api/requests/REQ-1001/team/submit
Content-Type: application/json

{ "userId": "alice", "confirmOnBehalf": true }

### 8) Statut côté service externe
GET {{host}}/mock-api/requests/REQ-1001

### 9a) Cas nominal : le trader confirme -> COMPLETED, rappels stoppés
POST {{host}}/api/requests/REQ-1001/trader/confirm

### 9b) Cas expiration : ne rien faire ~50 s (5 x 10 s) puis consulter emails + statut -> EXPIRED
GET {{host}}/api/requests/REQ-1001/emails

### 10) Panne du service externe -> le Submit crée un incident (Cockpit)
POST {{host}}/mock-api/fail?enabled=true

###
POST {{host}}/mock-api/fail?enabled=false
